      "message": "Initially this is what Nearby started with, but after discussion with the modularization team we ended up merging their API surface into framework-connectivity-t, see: https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Connectivity/framework-t/Android.bp;drc\u003d85de09411f91f1bf489851b328559e06cb459756;l\u003d44\n\nSo the Java API source file are there, but the API files are not (they\u0027re in https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Connectivity/framework-t/api/ together with the rest of the API exposed by the module).\n\nBut we should clarify whether your API should be exposed on T+ or U+ or V+; if one of the latter two, then it needs to be in a separate bootclasspath jar (framework-connectivity-v instead of framework-connectivity-t ?)",
